 e\nCategories: concert\, free\nSource: funcheap/san-francisco\n\nPhotojour
 nalists on the Front Lines of Protest: A panel discussion hosted by Indivi
 sible San Francisco and Pro Bono Photo. Indivisible SF presents a panel of
  local photojournalists from Pro Bono Photo and other news organizations w
 ho will share selections from their portfolios and discuss the role photoj
 ournalism plays in documenting protest\, civic action and pro-democracy mo
 vements. From the civil rights and voting rights movements of the 1960s to
  today’s social justice actions\, the San Francisco Bay Area has long be
 en a significant site of protest and civil disobedience. Who documents the
 se fleeting moments of protest and civic action? Local photojournalists sh
 are their experiences covering pro-democracy movements and street demonstr
 ations throughout the Bay Area. Hear firsthand accounts from photographers
  documenting recent protests and demonstrations\, view a curated projectio
 n of their work and engage directly with the panelists during an audience 
 Q&A. Pop-Up Gallery: A selection of photographs by participating photojour
 nalists will be displayed alongside historical protest photography from SF
 PL collections\, connecting contemporary documentation of Bay Area demonst
 rations with
